{
  "$comment": [
    "FND-04 deliverable 8. The PRD 16.2 and 16.3 endpoint lists, transcribed, plus the one endpoint",
    "PRD 34.3 names normatively and 16.2 omits (sub-PRD D24).",
    "",
    "`prd_line` is the PRD bullet VERBATIM, backticks included, so the Reviewer can read it beside",
    "docs/PRD.md character for character (ticket test-plan step 2). `derived: false` means the line",
    "already IS a path and a method; `derived: true` means sub-PRD D23's expansion rules produced the",
    "operations, and `basis` says which rule and why.",
    "",
    "PARAMETER NAMES. Where 16.2 spells the parameter, it is used verbatim ({document_id},",
    "{version_id}, {node_version_id}, {node_id}, {job_id}, {answer_snapshot_id}, and {id} for the",
    "three /v1/research-records sub-paths). Where a path is derived, the name is <resource>_id — with",
    "one deliberate exception: the derived /v1/research-records item path adopts {id} so that the",
    "resource is not spelled two ways in one tree.",
    "",
    "test/openapi/endpoint-replay.test.ts asserts BOTH directions: every operation here appears",
    "exactly once in schemas/openapi/openapi.yaml, and the document declares no operation absent from",
    "here. One direction alone is a vacuous check (FND-04 acceptance item 2)."
  ],
