    {
      "prd_section": "16.3",
      "group": "Authentication and machine access",
      "prd_line": "Invitation and membership lifecycle endpoints.",
      "derived": true,
      "basis": "Sub-PRD D23(e). A capability sentence, no path. Two nouns — invitation and membership — one collection each, lifecycle transitions as POST /{id}/<verb>. An invitation is created, listed, accepted and revoked; a membership is listed, read, role-changed and removed. Customer-visible path names remain the founder's to overrule (PRD 45.5).",
      "operations": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/invitations" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/invitations" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/invitations/{invitation_id}/accept" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/invitations/{invitation_id}/revoke" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/memberships" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/memberships/{membership_id}" },
        { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/v1/memberships/{membership_id}" },
        { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/v1/memberships/{membership_id}" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prd_section": "16.3",
      "group": "Authentication and machine access",
      "prd_line": "Session list/revoke and recent-authentication checks.",
      "derived": true,
      "basis": "Sub-PRD D23(e). \"list\" and \"revoke\" map to GET collection and DELETE item; the recent-authentication check is a created assertion, which is what clears 34.9's RECENT_AUTH_REQUIRED.",
      "operations": [
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/sessions" },
        { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/v1/sessions/{session_id}" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/recent-authentication-checks" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prd_section": "16.3",
      "group": "Authentication and machine access",
      "prd_line": "TOTP, passkey and recovery-code lifecycle.",
      "derived": true,
      "basis": "Sub-PRD D23(e). Three factors under one /v1/mfa prefix. TOTP is a single enrolment (no id): enrol, activate, remove. Passkeys are a collection: list, begin registration, activate, remove one. Recovery codes are regenerated as a set and returned once.",
      "operations": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/mfa/totp" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/mfa/totp/activate" },
        { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/v1/mfa/totp" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/mfa/passkeys" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/mfa/passkeys" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/mfa/passkeys/activate" },
        { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/v1/mfa/passkeys/{passkey_id}" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/mfa/recovery-codes" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prd_section": "16.3",
      "group": "Authentication and machine access",
      "prd_line": "SAML/OIDC SSO connection create/test/activate/disable.",
      "derived": true,
      "basis": "Sub-PRD D23(e). The four verbs are named by the sentence itself; create is POST collection and the other three are POST /{sso_connection_id}/<verb>. A list operation is added because the four verbs are unusable without one. The SsoConnectionState machine is 16.3's own.",
      "operations": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/sso-connections" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/sso-connections" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/sso-connections/{sso_connection_id}/test" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/sso-connections/{sso_connection_id}/activate" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/sso-connections/{sso_connection_id}/disable" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prd_section": "16.3",
      "group": "Authentication and machine access",
      "prd_line": "Service-account and credential create/rotate/revoke.",
      "derived": true,
      "basis": "Sub-PRD D23(e). A credential belongs to a service account, so it is a nested collection; rotate and revoke are named verbs on the credential. A service-account list operation is added because the credential paths are unusable without one.",
      "operations": [
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/service-accounts" },
        { "method": "GET", "path": "/v1/service-accounts" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/service-accounts/{service_account_id}/credentials" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/service-accounts/{service_account_id}/credentials/{credential_id}/rotate" },
        { "method": "POST", "path": "/v1/service-accounts/{service_account_id}/credentials/{credential_id}/revoke" }
      ]
    }
  ]
